<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 07:26:14 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Africa</category><title>Attackers target Niger's Niamey airport and presidency perimeter</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260829-attackers-target-niger-s-niamey-airport-and-presidency-perimeter</link><description>
Sustained gunfire and explosions rang out across several areas of Niger's capital, Niamey, early on Saturday, according to two Reuters witnesses, with the cause not immediately clear.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8708e288-6390-11f1-9bdc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/A%C3%A9roport-International-Diori-Hamani-de-Niamey-NIM-03.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8708e288-6390-11f1-9bdc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/A%C3%A9roport-International-Diori-Hamani-de-Niamey-NIM-03.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">423c7ca6-a377-11f1-a82a-25d87b3a8499</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 07:05:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8708e288-6390-11f1-9bdc-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/A%C3%A9roport-International-Diori-Hamani-de-Niamey-NIM-03.jpg">© Wikimedia Commons CC BY SA 4.0 Barke11</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Iceland referendum could put EU membership talks back on the table</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260829-iceland-referendum-could-put-eu-membership-talks-back-on-the-table</link><description>
Icelanders will vote on Saturday on whether to resume negotiations to join the European Union, with the result expected to be finely balanced after a campaign dominated by questions of sovereignty, fishing and the country’s place in an increasingly uncertain geopolitical landscape.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/191829e8-a29a-11f1-bd56-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239717725586.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/191829e8-a29a-11f1-bd56-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239717725586.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">32d2da14-a2b7-11f1-8c72-7d8b04e91d75</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 06:50:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/191829e8-a29a-11f1-bd56-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239717725586.jpg">© AP Photo/Marco Di Marco</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>‘Words and promises not enough’ as Syria’s Kurds face uncertain future</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260828-words-and-promises-are-not-enough-as-syria-s-kurds-face-uncertain-future</link><description>
Syria’s Kurds are facing an uncertain future after this week’s dissolution of the Kurdish-led Syrian Democratic Forces and the integration of military and civilian institutions in northeastern Syria into the Syrian state, raising questions over what the changes will mean for their rights, safety and daily lives. RFI spoke to a Kurdish civil society activist in the region.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8842c9ae-a222-11f1-a5b3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4B68KG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8842c9ae-a222-11f1-a5b3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4B68KG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7b92699e-a218-11f1-8110-418826f8ad24</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:05:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8842c9ae-a222-11f1-a5b3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4B68KG.jpg">AFP - DELIL SOULEIMAN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Nepal’s deadly glacier collapse exposes climate risks across the Himalayas</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260827-nepal-s-deadly-glacier-collapse-exposes-climate-risks-across-the-himalayas</link><description>
A massive glacier collapse that triggered deadly flooding on the Nepal-Tibet border has exposed the growing dangers facing the rapidly warming Himalayas, where scientists say retreating ice and thawing ground are making mountain landscapes increasingly unstable.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4310f710-a20a-11f1-bc15-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T020731Z-574437780-RC2P6NAPHNWT-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4310f710-a20a-11f1-bc15-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T020731Z-574437780-RC2P6NAPHNWT-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e5c1da20-a222-11f1-af26-f7f1b19f1d48</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:01:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4310f710-a20a-11f1-bc15-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T020731Z-574437780-RC2P6NAPHNWT-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg">© REUTERS - Navesh Chitrakar </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron to meet new UK PM Burnham against backdrop of Bayeux Tapestry</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260828-macron-to-meet-new-uk-pm-burnham-against-backdrop-of-bayeux-tapestry</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron will travel to London on Wednesday for his first meeting with the United Kingdom's new prime minister, Andy Burnham, in what will be the first visit by a European Union leader since he took office. Macron will also unveil the Bayeux Tapestry at the British Museum in a "significant moment" for Franco-British relations. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d03d4b4c-60a3-11f0-bc9e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-66AF26N.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d03d4b4c-60a3-11f0-bc9e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-66AF26N.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5cad6ee0-a2d9-11f1-9f07-57f96fb022cb</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:47:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d03d4b4c-60a3-11f0-bc9e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-66AF26N.jpg">AFP - GONZALO FUENTES</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French presidential hopefuls clash over economy and EU in first debate</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260828-french-presidential-hopefuls-clash-over-economy-and-eu-in-first-debate</link><description>
Seven leading candidates in the race to succeed President Emmanuel Macron have clashed in their first debate ahead of the 2027 election, exposing sharp differences over the economy, public debt and France's relationship with the European Union.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/309dabde-a2c6-11f1-ad7b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T162935Z-59374920-RC227NATGZTL-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-BUSINESS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/309dabde-a2c6-11f1-ad7b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T162935Z-59374920-RC227NATGZTL-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-BUSINESS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">872c426c-a2c6-11f1-82aa-99d519c5795b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:07:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/309dabde-a2c6-11f1-ad7b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T162935Z-59374920-RC227NATGZTL-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-BUSINESS.jpg">REUTERS - Stephanie Lecocq</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Algeria mourns wildfire victims as firefighters battle deadly blazes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260828-algeria-mourns-wildfire-victims-as-firefighters-battle-deadly-blazes</link><description>
Algeria entered a second day of national mourning on Friday as firefighters continued to battle wildfires in the north of the country that have killed at least 12 people and injured dozens.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ec57c822-a263-11f1-a811-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239683873317.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ec57c822-a263-11f1-a811-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239683873317.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7683abda-a2ad-11f1-95b2-8b24c41db7b3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 10:01:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ec57c822-a263-11f1-a811-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239683873317.jpg">© AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French Foreign Legion soldier kidnapped by Colombian guerrilla faction</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260828-french-foreign-legion-soldier-kidnapped-in-southwestern-colombia-guerilla</link><description>
The Colombian army has announced that a soldier in the French Foreign Legion was kidnapped earlier this month while travelling through Narino, a region in southwestern Colombia dominated by guerrillas.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/560a40de-1f61-11ef-99d1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34U984T.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/560a40de-1f61-11ef-99d1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34U984T.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21af97f2-a2a5-11f1-acd2-a97c7d4b6ac3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 06:49:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/560a40de-1f61-11ef-99d1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34U984T.jpg">AFP - DELPHINE MAYEUR</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Serb war criminal Mladic, dubbed the ‘Butcher of Bosnia,’ dies aged 84</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260827-bosnian-serb-war-criminal-dubbed-the-butcher-of-bosnia-dies-aged-84</link><description>
Ratko Mladic, the former Bosnian Serb military chief convicted of war crimes for his role in the 1995 Srebrenica massacre, died in hospital on Thursday, according to a United Nations international tribunal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d2d1841a-a22c-11f1-96f9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T142848Z-1358587860-RC227NA3MIE4-RTRMADP-3-PEOPLE-RATKO-MLADIC-REACTIONS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d2d1841a-a22c-11f1-96f9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T142848Z-1358587860-RC227NA3MIE4-RTRMADP-3-PEOPLE-RATKO-MLADIC-REACTIONS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac9259c4-a230-11f1-8f4a-8f6ffdc70ead</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:02:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d2d1841a-a22c-11f1-96f9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T142848Z-1358587860-RC227NA3MIE4-RTRMADP-3-PEOPLE-RATKO-MLADIC-REACTIONS.jpg">©  Chris Helgren / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Cop17 races for desertification deal as report warns half world’s soils under threat</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260828-cop17-soil-governance-essential-to-global-deal-on-combatting-drought</link><description>
Delegates at the Cop17 summit on desertification in Mongolia are seeking to seal a deal to combat drought on Friday, the last day of the event – as a United Nations report warns the world's soils are rapidly deteriorating, while tried and tested solutions are not being implemented. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4ff49786-7382-11f1-9445-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8EN6N4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4ff49786-7382-11f1-9445-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8EN6N4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">28015e30-a226-11f1-84a1-f7f1b19f1d48</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 05:29:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4ff49786-7382-11f1-9445-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8EN6N4.jpg">© STEFANO RELLANDINI / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Haiti families plead for release of hostages after deadly gang attack</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260827-haiti-families-plead-for-release-of-hostages-after-deadly-gang-attack</link><description>
Families in Kenscoff near the Haitian capital Port-au-Prince are demanding the release of relatives taken hostage by armed gangs during last weekend's deadly attack on the town. At least 47 people were killed and more than 20 abducted, with thousands having fled their homes to avoid further attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/60da7c5c-a1cf-11f1-94b7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T205531Z-633498750-RC225NAK43KW-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/60da7c5c-a1cf-11f1-94b7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T205531Z-633498750-RC225NAK43KW-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e25ceed8-a204-11f1-937e-4918512faead</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 14:02:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/60da7c5c-a1cf-11f1-94b7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T205531Z-633498750-RC225NAK43KW-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE.jpg">REUTERS - Patrice Noel</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Former model sues French state over delay in Epstein recruiter rape investigation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-former-model-sues-french-state-over-delay-in-epstein-recruiter-rape-investigation</link><description>
A former model who accused an alleged recruiter for American sex offender Jeffrey Epstein of raping her in the 1990s is suing the French state for delays to the investigation. The state is also being sued by a child protection organisation, on behalf of alleged Epstein victims.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fd9e7c3a-a190-11f1-b354-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A3WX7QX.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fd9e7c3a-a190-11f1-b354-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A3WX7QX.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">25d4ac50-a214-11f1-8343-418826f8ad24</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 14:03:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fd9e7c3a-a190-11f1-b354-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A3WX7QX.jpg">© Joel Saget/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France to tie African development aid to efforts to limit migration to Mayotte</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-france-to-tie-african-development-aid-to-efforts-to-limit-migration-to-mayotte</link><description>
France plans to make its development aid to seven African countries conditional on greater cooperation in the fight against illegal immigration to the French island territory of Mayotte, as the issue becomes increasingly politicised ahead of the French presidential election next year.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98391ee4-a15a-11f1-ac0e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6866ZR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98391ee4-a15a-11f1-ac0e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6866ZR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aa5d8488-a200-11f1-b7e4-dd9f6f304afc</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:30:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98391ee4-a15a-11f1-ac0e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6866ZR.jpg">© Marine Gachet/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Looking up: French sailors ditch GPS to rediscover celestial art of navigation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-looking-up-french-sailors-ditch-gps-to-rediscover-celestial-art-of-navigation</link><description>
Astronaut Sophie Adenot made history this month as the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Back on Earth, space enthusiasts across France are finding their own ways to reach for the stars. In the fourth of a five-part series, RFI meets amateur sailors learning to navigate by the stars, using a technique that allows them to find their position without GPS or onboard electronics.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4247340c-a151-11f1-9f33-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Margo-l-un-des-quatre-stagiaires-%C3%A0-bord-du-Whirlwind-s-exerce-%C3%A0-la-manipulation-du-sextant.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4247340c-a151-11f1-9f33-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Margo-l-un-des-quatre-stagiaires-%C3%A0-bord-du-Whirlwind-s-exerce-%C3%A0-la-manipulation-du-sextant.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4d36764e-a1f5-11f1-b80f-89dd84255de2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 14:03:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4247340c-a151-11f1-9f33-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Margo-l-un-des-quatre-stagiaires-%C3%A0-bord-du-Whirlwind-s-exerce-%C3%A0-la-manipulation-du-sextant.jpg">© Baptiste Coulon / RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Second person dies after man deliberately drives into crowd in Caen</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-second-person-dies-after-man-deliberately-drives-into-crowd-in-caen</link><description>
A second person has died after a man deliberately drove his car into a group of people in the northern French city of Caen on Wednesday, leaving nine others injured.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4f546802-a1fd-11f1-b51b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6L439E.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4f546802-a1fd-11f1-b51b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6L439E.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f623464-a1f8-11f1-864a-d35118897ed7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:06:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4f546802-a1fd-11f1-b51b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6L439E.jpg">AFP - MATTHIEU CLAVEL</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Nigerian armed groups net nearly $6m in ransoms: study</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260826-nigerian-armed-groups-net-nearly-6-mn-in-ransoms-study</link><description>
Criminal groups in Nigeria raised nearly $6 million in ransom payments in the last year, a report said Wednesday, with two mass kidnappings by Boko Haram responsible for nearly 90 percent of the total.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/55d8be7a-a195-11f1-b953-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/6961939120bd9f4ef8b93ca57cd743048790f5a8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/55d8be7a-a195-11f1-b953-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/6961939120bd9f4ef8b93ca57cd743048790f5a8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56fe9964-a195-11f1-a31a-95a8899ba87e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:30:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/55d8be7a-a195-11f1-b953-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/6961939120bd9f4ef8b93ca57cd743048790f5a8.jpg">© Ifeanyi Immanuel Bakwenye / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France relaxes rules for three famous cheeses after summer drought</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-france-relaxes-rules-for-three-famous-cheeses-after-summer-drought</link><description>
The drought in France is forcing farmers who produce milk for some of the country's most famous cheeses to feed their cows differently, as scorched pastures make it increasingly difficult to stick to strict rules on protected regional foods, known as AOP. Temporary exemptions on fodder sources will apply to the producers of Abondance, Beaufort and Comté to cope with the grass shortage.
